--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@ The bundle is written to `ios/Resources/KiriEngine/kiri-snapslice.js`. Review ch
 - Built for iPhone and the Snapmaker U1. Printer functions need the U1 to be reachable, normally on the same Wi-Fi network; the app has no internet relay or background push service.
 - The on-device slicer can run slowly or run out of memory on very large/complex models. Progress and errors appear in the app, but progress is not a reliable time estimate.
 - STL and supported 3MF geometry, parts, and painted colors are imported. Creator-specific print profiles, modifiers, and some 3MF variants do not transfer. Confirm settings and tool mapping before printing.
+- On compatible LiDAR iPhones, **Escanear objeto em 3D** guides a middle, upper, and flipped underside photo pass using RealityKit Object Capture. Reconstruction runs on the iPhone and produces a millimeter STL for the Prepare view. It uses the on-device reduced-detail mode; the STL has no color or texture. Check scale, base, and mesh defects before slicing. Capture does not guarantee a watertight printable model. Source photos and the USDZ remain under Files > SnapSlice > Scans.
 - Four-color printing requires matching the chosen T1–T4 assignments with the filament actually loaded. Material combinations and support interfaces are not automatically validated.
 - The camera shows refreshed still images. Repository shortcuts open the providers' websites; there is no combined model search or profile converter yet.
 
